mareader-g2p ports the English grapheme-to-phoneme pipeline of loqui-g2p 0.4.0
to read its data from downloaded files.

  loqui-g2p — https://github.com/Awakened-Labs/loqui
  Copyright (c) 2026 Awakened Labs Inc. MIT License.

The pipeline it ports, and the data the app downloads at run time from
Awakened-Labs/loqui at commit 717691aadf67408c85d87dc33e5d1d77b2ea4b4d:

  misaki English G2P logic and lexicons, version 0.9.4 (us/gb gold and
  silver) — https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki
  Apache License 2.0.

  spaCy English tokenizer rules (spaCy 3.8) — https://github.com/explosion/spaCy
  Copyright (c) 2016-2026 ExplosionAI GmbH, 2016 spaCy GmbH, 2015 Matthew
  Honnibal. MIT License. The tokenizer algorithm is reimplemented.

  Part-of-speech tagger weights (tagger-en.bin), original to loqui, trained on
  public-domain text labelled by spaCy's MIT-licensed en_core_web_sm. MIT.

  Grapheme-to-phoneme BART models trained on the misaki lexicons:
    https://huggingface.co/PeterReid/graphemes_to_phonemes_en_us
    https://huggingface.co/PeterReid/graphemes_to_phonemes_en_gb
  Apache License 2.0.

  Number wording follows num2words 0.5.14 (LGPL); none of its code is used.

No GPL code is used: where misaki asks eSpeak NG about unknown words, the
BART model answers instead.
